WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
The first film tested inheritance models against family observations.

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.120
How can learning that someone is unaffected raise their carrier probability?

3
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:16.060
The surprise comes from comparing only genotypes still compatible with the

4
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.060
observation.

5
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.990
Begin with every genotype the inheritance model allows.

6
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.610
Give each possibility its starting weight before using the person's phenotype.

7
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.010
These weights come from transmission rules and any population assumptions.

8
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.490
Write them down before looking at the answer you hope to get.

9
00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:42.613
Now condition on what you observed.

10
00:00:43.993 --> 00:00:48.233
Any genotype incompatible with that observation loses its weight.

11
00:00:49.653 --> 00:00:51.353
Compatible possibilities remain.

12
00:00:52.573 --> 00:00:55.573
This is a filter, not a change to the person's cells.

13
00:00:56.893 --> 00:00:59.473
Keep the survivors in their original proportions.

14
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:04.947
Suppose a new observation excludes one visible possibility.

15
00:01:06.227 --> 00:01:10.487
Which tiles should remain in the probability bar, and what must happen next?

16
00:01:11.707 --> 00:01:14.547
Watch the total bar, not just the disappearing tile.

17
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:22.573
Remove the incompatible tile.

18
00:01:23.813 --> 00:01:26.553
Then stretch the survivors to fill the whole bar again.

19
00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.893
That second step is renormalizing.

20
00:01:31.153 --> 00:01:35.593
The surviving possibilities now divide all the probability between them.

21
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:40.323
A carrier tile can therefore occupy more of the remaining bar.

22
00:01:41.523 --> 00:01:44.143
This can happen even when the person is unaffected.

23
00:01:45.443 --> 00:01:47.263
The comparison set became smaller.

24
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.573
Nothing happened to the person's DNA.

25
00:01:52.173 --> 00:01:55.513
Evidence changes genotype probabilities, not genotypes.

26
00:01:56.873 --> 00:01:59.213
Only the description of your uncertainty changed.

27
00:02:00.283 --> 00:02:03.523
Sometimes evidence does not eliminate a hypothesis.

28
00:02:04.943 --> 00:02:08.323
It is merely more likely under one hypothesis than another.

29
00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.283
Bayes' rule handles that case.

30
00:02:12.523 --> 00:02:17.283
The observation changes weights without making either hypothesis impossible.

31
00:02:18.723 --> 00:02:20.683
Likelihood measures that predictive fit.

32
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:24.313
Each hypothesis starts with a prior weight.

33
00:02:25.773 --> 00:02:29.833
Multiply that weight by how well the hypothesis predicts the observation.

34
00:02:31.093 --> 00:02:34.073
A better prediction earns a larger updated weight.

35
00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:36.853
A weak prediction earns less.

36
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:40.937
Finally, renormalize those weighted hypotheses.

37
00:02:42.377 --> 00:02:47.077
Their new shares form the posterior: the probabilities after accounting for the

38
00:02:47.077 --> 00:02:52.117
evidence. Together, those shares still fill the complete probability bar.

39
00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.907
More observations repeat the same cycle.

40
00:02:57.267 --> 00:03:01.507
Start with current weights, ask what each hypothesis predicts, apply the evidence,

41
00:03:01.887 --> 00:03:06.167
then renormalize. Each new fact becomes the next filter.

42
00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.887
The method remains the same.

43
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.080
The answer still depends on the model.

44
00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:19.260
Penetrance, new mutation, family relationships, and population assumptions all shape

45
00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.660
those starting weights and likelihoods.

46
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:26.700
If an assumption changes, recompute instead of reusing the old answer.

47
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.230
With that picture, the text can calculate exact carrier and recurrence

48
00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:37.270
probabilities. Keep the filter, the weights, and the assumptions visible.

49
00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.590
The worked examples begin with different family evidence.
